ume | unique open (phone, purpose) |\n| `auth_sessions` | Refresh hash, expiry, revoke | unique refresh hash |\n| `employee_invites` | Opaque hashed invite | unique active invite per employee |\n\n## Alters\n| Change | Existing data | Notes |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `users.profile_completed_at` nullable | all NULL | ORM currently does not map this column so 0007 tests keep running |\n| `employees.user_id` nullable | existing rows stay non-null | unique(user_id) still allows multiple unbound NULLs |\n| `work_order_assignments.assigned_source` default HUMAN | backfill HUMAN | `assigned_by_user_id` nullable; CHECK HUMAN requires actor, AUTO requires NULL |\n| `work_order_assignments.payload_json` | NULL | score/filter snapshot |\n| `ai_call_logs.provider_mode` | backfill DEVELOPMENT | DEVELOPMENT vs PRODUCTION evidence split |\n\n## Outbox / claim\nNo outbox table in 0009. Auto-assign currently runs in the analysis transaction. Durable enqueue remains the reserved 0008 plan.\n\n## Apply / regress\n- Do **not** upgrade `property_ai` or `property_ai_day4`.\n- Disposable `TEST_DATABASE_URL` upgrade requires an explicit operator approval.\n- Downgrade drops new tables and reverses alters; it will fail if unbound employees or AUTO assignments exist.\n\n## ORM note\nAssignment AUTO columns and `ai_call_logs.provider_mode` are in the draft SQL but not yet mapped, so current 0007 integration tests keep inserting assignments/call logs. Auto-dispatch returns `SCHEMA_PENDING_0009` until those columns are mapped after an approved upgrade.\n\nFILE: reports/auth-identity-ai-001\\live-provider-results.json\n{\n  \"status\": \"NOT_RUN\",\n  \"reason\": \"No authorized live credentials. Paid SMS/models were not invoked.\",\n  \"wechat_jscode2session\": \"NOT_RUN\",\n  \"sms_carrier\": \"NOT_RUN\",\n  \"realname\": \"NOT_RUN\",\n  \"llm\": \"NOT_RUN\",\n  \"vlm\": \"NOT_RUN\",\n  \"asr\": \"NOT_RUN\",\n  \"embedding\": \"NOT_RUN\",\n  \"reranker\": \"NOT_RUN\"\n}\n\nFILE: reports/auth-identity-ai-001\\evidence-boundary.md\n# Evidence boundary �� AUTH-IDENTITY-AI-001\n\nVIS-001..004 remain local visualization only. They used DevAuth seed login and Fake providers.\n\n| Claim | Status |\n| --- | --- |\n| Unified login page with SMS/password fields calling `/auth/sms/*` and `/auth/password/*` | Software implemented. Not formally accepted. |\n| Real credential verification (not `/auth/dev/token`) | Backend routes implemented. Formal login.js does not call DevAuth except LOCAL_PREVIEW. Runtime DB tests skip until 0009. |\n| OTP attempts persist before 401 | `_apply_otp` then commit then `_raise_otp`. |\n| Redis throttle | Lua INCR+EXPIRE, fail-closed. |\n| WeChat unknown openid | `AUTH.WECHAT_BIND_REQUIRED`, no User insert. |\n| WeChat bind | Requires Principal.auth_method sms or password. |\n| WeChat known-binding login | Issues AuthSession + refresh. Needs 0009 table. |\n| Formal admin employee `user_id` | Rejected when APP_ENV not development/test. |\n| Mini-program session restore | 401 refresh-once then retry, shared in-flight refresh. Credential-auth 401 does not clear session. |\n| Development SMS labeled | `delivery_channel=development`. Not real SMS. |\n| Formal house picker without typed house_id | Mini-program cascading selectors. Catalog GET routes exist. |\n| Employee invite/claim | Software implemented. Needs 0009 `employee_invites`. |\n| Automatic Assignment without human assign tap | **Not complete.** `ai_auto_assign` default False. Pipeline returns `SCHEMA_PENDING_0009` until assignment source columns are applied and mapped. |\n| Real LLM/VLM/ASR/Embedding | NOT_RUN. Adapters exist. Day 4 still Fake. |\n| Production V1 / Day 4 PASS | Not claimed. |\n\nDo not treat HTTP 200, ANALYZE events, or citation arrays as real-AI completion.\n\n\ncodex\n{\"task_id\":\"AUTH-IDENTITY-AI-001\",\"phase\":\"review\",\"reviewed_head\":\"38d3d09\",\"decision\":\"READY\",\"actions_or_findings\":[{\"title\":\"Evidence loaded\",\"path\":\"reports/auth-identity-ai-001\",\"trigger\":\"Round 3 evidence review\",\"rationale\":\"The reports preserve the required boundary: no persistent 0009 migration, no live-provider run, and no formal auth/real-AI/Production V1 claim. I’m now checking the actual working tree rather than accepting report assertions.\"}],\"evidence_paths\":[\"reports/project-handoff.md\",\"reports/auth-identity-ai-001/evidence-boundary.md\",\"reports/auth-identity-ai-001/software-test-results.json\",\"reports/auth-identity-ai-001/schema-review.md\",\"reports/auth-identity-ai-001/live-provider-results.json\"],\"unverified\":[\"Round 2 code remediations\",\"Round 1 regression constraints\",\"Authorized-slice defects\"],\"session_note\":\"Reports read; source inspection underway.\"}\nexec\n\"C:\\\\WINDOWS\\\\System32\\\\WindowsPowerShell\\\\v1.0\\\\powershell.exe\" -Command \"Get-Content -LiteralPath 'reports/codex/AUTH-IDENTITY-AI-001-plan.json' -Raw -Encoding utf8; Get-Content -LiteralPath 'reports/codex/AUTH-IDENTITY-AI-001-review.json' -Raw -Encoding utf8; Get-Content -LiteralPath 'reports/codex/AUTH-IDENTITY-AI-001-review.prompt.txt' -Raw -Encoding utf8\" in D:\\property-ai\n succeeded in 143ms:\n{\"task_id\":\"AUTH-IDENTITY-AI-001\",\"phase\":\"plan\",\"reviewed_head\":\"38d3d09bf2e27154c4d106403cbfa9619026755a\",\"decision\":\"READY\",\"actions_or_findings\":[{\"title\":\"1. Implement official credential authentication and draft migration 0009\",\"path\":\"D:\\\\property-ai\\\\backend\\\\alembic\\\\versions\\\\20260919_0009_official_auth_identity_dispatch.py\",\"trigger\":\"Current authentication supports only Development and WeChat JWTs; SMS/password/session revocation are absent, and unknown WeChat identities silently create Users.\",\"rationale\":\"Draft revision 20260919_0009 with down_revision=20260917_0007; do not modify 0001-0007, occupy 0008, or apply it to any persistent database. Add User.profile_completed_at, user_phones with verified history and phone uniqueness, user_passwords with one Argon2id credential per User, sms_challenges with keyed code hash/TTL/attempts/consumed_at, and auth_sessions with hashed rotating refresh tokens, auth_method, expiry, and revocation. Implement atomic Redis send/login throttles through an injectable limiter that fails closed; unit tests must use a fake and must not touch Redis. OTPs must be random per challenge, one-time, retry-limited, never returned by formal APIs, and never logged; the Development SMS provider must be explicitly labeled and test-capturable without becoming real-SMS evidence. Implement /auth/sms/send, /auth/sms/login, /auth/password/login, /auth/password/change, /auth/password/reset, /auth/token/refresh, and /auth/logout across model/identity.py, schema/auth.py, service/auth.py or a focused credential_auth.py, repository/identity.py, provider/sms, provider/factory.py, core/security.py, core/config.py, and core/errors.py. OTP login may create one User only after phone proof and uniqueness locking; password login never creates one. Formal JWTs use auth_method sms|password, a server-checked session identifier, and current database authorization; password reset/change revoke all old sessions and issue a fresh session only after successful verification. Known WeChat bindings may receive session-backed auth_method=wechat tokens; an unknown openid must return bind-required without inserting User/UserWechat, then bind only after an authenticated phone/password session exchanges a fresh WeChat code. Conflicts require later controlled merge, never auto-merge. Update the mini-program login flow to real SMS/password actions, validated /me restoration and refresh rotation; keep Seed login only under explicit LOCAL_PREVIEW and ensure no formal handler calls /auth/dev/token. Router mounting and token verification must independently reject Development Auth outside development/test. If reserved 0008 lands before migration approval, retarget 0009 to revise 0008; otherwise 0008 must later revise 0009��never create sibling heads.\"},{\"title\":\"2. Add safe house catalog APIs and remove raw house_id from the formal UI\",\"path\":\"D:\\\\property-ai\\\\backend\\\\app\\\\api\\\\v1\\\\property_catalog.py\",\"trigger\":\"PropertyRepository contains hierarchy queries, but no catalog HTTP routes exist and the current mini-program bind form requires a typed house_id.\",\"rationale\":\"Add authenticated GET /properties, /properties/{id}/buildings, /buildings/{id}/units, and /units/{id}/houses using repository/service methods that derive tenant/property ancestry from stored parents rather than trusting client scope. Return only safe physical catalog fields, filter inactive Tenant/House records, and never join or expose resident names, phones, relationships, bind requests, or work orders. Add PATCH /me/profile for display_name and profile completion. Rework pages/houses into cascading property/building/unit/room selectors; the selected internal house ID may be submitted to the unchanged POST /resident-bind-requests API, but no formal text input may accept house_id. Preserve existing manager approve/reject APIs. Tests must prove unauthenticated denial, parent-scope validation, absence of resident data, pending bind state, and that catalog visibility does not authorize work-order creation or resident resources before approval.\"},{\"title\":\"3. Bind an authenticated User to an existing Employee through a controlled claim\",\"path\":\"D:\\\\property-ai\\\\backend\\\\app\\\\service\\\\employee_identity.py\",\"trigger\":\"POST /admin/employees currently requires client-supplied user_id; no invite or ownership-verification flow exists.\",\"rationale\":\"In 0009 make employees.user_id nullable while retaining the unique FK for claimed employees; existing non-null records remain unchanged. Add employee_invites with BIGINT identity, employee/tenant scope, target phone, hashed random claim token, inviter, expiry, retry/status, claimant, consumed_at, and uniqueness for one active invite per Employee. Permit administrators with current employee:manage scope to create an unbound Employee and separately issue/revoke/resend its invite; keep direct user attachment only in internal Development fixtures. The authenticated claim endpoint must lock invite and Employee, require an active verified UserPhone matching the target, reject expiry/replay/disabled Employee/duplicate binding, and set employee.user_id exactly once. Resolve Role by code STAFF and grant only scopes derived from current EmployeeProperty rows in the same transaction; never accept user_id, role, tenant/property scope, or employee_no as claim authority. Add a mini-program employee-claim page accepting only the opaque invitation. Tests must cover a different authenticated User, employee_no-only input, disabled Employee, expired/replayed invite, duplicate claim, cross-tenant manager, and permission revocation affecting an already-issued session.\"},{\"title\":\"4. Wire deterministic auto-assignment behind ai_auto_assign\",\"path\":\"D:\\\\property-ai\\\\backend\\\\app\\\\service\\\\auto_dispatch.py\",\"trigger\":\"AnalysisService writes deterministic recommendations but always stops at PENDING_ASSIGNMENT; WorkOrderAssignment currently requires a human assigned_by_user_id.\",\"rationale\":\"Extend 0009 to backfill work_order_assignments.assigned_source=HUMAN, make assigned_by_user_id nullable, add payload_json, and enforce HUMAN requires an actor while AUTO requires assigned_by_user_id NULL. Update response schemas accordingly. Also add ai_call_logs.provider_mode with DEVELOPMENT|PRODUCTION and backfill current rows DEVELOPMENT so Fake and real evidence cannot be mixed. When settings.ai_auto_assign is true, call a transactional auto-dispatch service after validated, non-low-confidence, non-high-risk analysis and recommendation generation. It must lock the WorkOrder and selected EmployeeDailyStatus, re-run active User/STAFF role, Employee, EmployeeProperty, duty/skill, on-duty, property and capacity checks, then atomically create the AUTO Assignment, increment load, set current_assignment_id, transition to ASSIGNED, and write SYSTEM WorkOrderLog/AuditLog entries with actor_user_id NULL and the analysis/rank/score/filter snapshot. It must never consume employee_id from LLM output. Disabled setting, low confidence, non-none risk, provider failure, invalid output, no candidate, revoked/disabled employee, or concurrency conflict must retain the appropriate PENDING_ANALYSIS or PENDING_ASSIGNMENT human queue with an explicit reason. Preserve human assign/reassign as HUMAN. Keep ai_auto_assign=False in persistent configuration and add no outbox/claim table; document the future outbox transaction boundary in the schema review.\"},{\"title\":\"5. Add negative-path tests and evidence boundaries\",\"path\":\"D:\\\\property-ai\\\\backend\\\\tests\",\"trigger\":\"Historical VIS and Development-provider results do not prove official authentication, automatic Assignment creation, or real AI.\",\"rationale\":\"Add focused unit/static tests runnable without external state and DB-backed integration tests staged for later disposable-DB approval. Required cases: wrong password; wrong, expired, exhausted, and replayed OTP; SMS limits; Argon2id storage; refresh replay; password reset/change session revocation; unknown WeChat causing no User side effect; unauthorized identity switching; production DevAuth route and existing-token rejection; catalog data minimization; unapproved house access; disabled Employee; live permission revocation; default-off auto-dispatch; enabled safe-result auto-dispatch creating WorkOrderAssignment without the human assign endpoint; no-candidate/high-risk/low-confidence/provider-failure fallbacks; concurrent assignment/capacity behavior; and rejection of an LLM employee_id field. Provider evidence must show mode, provider/model identity, validated structured output and downstream state; adapter construction, HTTP 200, ANALYZE, or citations alone are insufficient. Record exact commands, SHA, passed/failed/skipped counts and environment classification in software-test-results.json. Keep live-provider-results.json as NOT_RUN until credentials and authorization exist. Migration upgrade/downgrade and runtime integration tests must wait for an explicitly approved disposable database and must never target property_ai/property_ai_day4 or recreate mysql-test.\"}],\"evidence_paths\":[\"D:\\\\property-ai\\\\backend\\\\alembic\\\\versions\\\\20260919_0009_official_auth_identity_dispatch.py\",\"D:\\\\property-ai\\\\backend\\\\app\\\\service\\\\credential_auth.py\",\"D:\\\\property-ai\\\\backend\\\\app\\\\api\\\\v1\\\\property_catalog.py\",\"D:\\\\property-ai\\\\backend\\\\app\\\\service\\\\employee_identity.py\",\"D:\\\\property-ai\\\\backend\\\\app\\\\service\\\\auto_dispatch.py\",\"D:\\\\property-ai\\\\backend\\\\tests\\\\unit\\\\test_official_auth_security.py\",\"D:\\\\property-ai\\\\backend\\\\tests\\\\unit\\\\test_ai_evidence_provenance.py\",\"D:\\\\property-ai\\\\backend\\\\tests\\\\integration\\\\test_auth_identity_dispatch_migration.py\",\"D:\\\\property-ai\\\\backend\\\\tests\\\\integration\\\\test_official_auth_runtime.py\",\"D:\\\\property-ai\\\\backend\\\\tests\\\\integration\\\\test_house_catalog_runtime.py\",\"D:\\\\property-ai\\\\backend\\\\tests\\\\integration\\\\test_employee_claim_runtime.py\",\"D:\\\\property-ai\\\\backend\\\\tests\\\\integration\\\\test_auto_assignment_runtime.py\",\"D:\\\\property-ai\\\\miniprogram\\\\pages\\\\login\\\\login.js\",\"D:\\\\property-ai\\\\miniprogram\\\\pages\\\\login\\\\login.wxml\",\"D:\\\\property-ai\\\\miniprogram\\\\pages\\\\profile\\\\profile.js\",\"D:\\\\property-ai\\\\miniprogram\\\\pages\\\\profile\\\\profile.wxml\",\"D:\\\\property-ai\\\\miniprogram\\\\pages\\\\houses\\\\houses.js\",\"D:\\\\property-ai\\\\miniprogram\\\\pages\\\\houses\\\\houses.wxml\",\"D:\\\\property-ai\\\\miniprogram\\\\pages\\\\employee-claim\\\\employee-claim.js\",\"D:\\\\property-ai\\\\miniprogram\\\\pages\\\\employee-claim\\\\employee-claim.wxml\",\"D:\\\\property-ai\\\\reports\\\\auth-identity-ai-001\\\\schema-review.md\",\"D:\\\\property-ai\\\\reports\\\\auth-identity-ai-001\\\\software-test-results.json\",\"D:\\\\property-ai\\\\reports\\\\auth-identity-ai-001\\\\evidence-boundary.md\",\"D:\\\\property-ai\\\\reports\\\\auth-identity-ai-001\\\\live-provider-results.json\",\"D:\\\\property-ai\\\\reports\\\\codex\\\\AUTH-IDENTITY-AI-001-plan.json\",\"D:\\\\property-ai\\\\reports\\\\codex\\\\AUTH-IDENTITY-AI-001-review.prompt.txt\",\"D:\\\\property-ai\\\\reports\\\\codex\\\\AUTH-IDENTITY-AI-001-review.json\"],\"unverified\":[\"Migration 0009 has not been created, applied, upgraded, downgraded, or regression-tested against any database. Disposable and persistent database migration require separate explicit approval.\",\"Real WeChat jscode2session, paid SMS delivery, real-name verification, Qwen LLM/VLM, ASR, bge-m3 embedding, reranker, and all other live-provider calls remain NOT_RUN pending credentials and authorization.\",\"ai_auto_assign remains False in persistent environments; enabling it there requires a separate operator decision after migration and concurrency evidence.\",\"Phone change, explicit WeChat rebind, controlled account merge, and high-risk real-name recovery remain tracked Production V1 gaps and must not be removed from the handoff.\",\"VIS-001..004 remain local visualization evidence only. Day 4 release and Production V1 PASS remain unverified.\"],\"session_note\":\"READY for independent source, migration-draft, UI, and test-authoring work. This review changed nothing and ran no tests or external services.\"}\n{\"task_id\":\"AUTH-IDENTITY-AI-001\",\"phase\":\"review\",\"reviewed_head\":\"38d3d09bf2e27154c4d106403cbfa9619026755a\",\"decision\":\"NEEDS_CHANGES\",\"actions_or_findings\":[{\"title\":\"Round-1 remediations 1-5 and 7 are present\",\"path\":\"D:\\\\property-ai\",\"trigger\":\"Static inspection of the current working tree\",\"rationale\"